// Chains of Mechanus

@0 = ~Golden Chain~
@1 = ~Chains of Mechanus~

@10 = ~The chain links seem to be made from gold and are held together by an unknown force.

STATISTICS:

Weight: 2~
@11 = ~These chains are made from golden adamantine and several unidentified materials, which are held together by resilient threads of energy.

They were once part of a colossal modron engine that calculated the prediction that free will was statistically impossible. However, the engine was destroyed by agents from Limbo before it could prove its conclusion. Many parts of the destroyed engine, including these chains, were blown across the planes by the force of the explosion. Several years later they were discovered by a scouting party of the Revolutionary League on Acheron and brought back to Sigil.

The inherent magic of the item reacts strongly to the ethical belief of the wearer. The more it deviates from pure law and logic the more it "fights" against the will of the wearer and impairs their concentration.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
– Lawful: +2 bonus to armor class and saving throws
– Neutral: Random bonus between 0 and +2 to armor class and saving throws
– Chaotic: Random penalty or bonus between -2 and +2 to armor class and saving throws

– Aura of Coordination:  Allies within 8 ft. radius of the wearer are affected by a weaker effect
  Lawful: +1 bonus to armor class and saving throws
  Neutral: 50% chance of +1 bonus to armor class and saving throws
  Chaotic: Random penalty or bonus between -1 and +1 to armor class and saving throws

Weight: 2~

@20 = ~Aura of Coordination~
